264 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (The first map visualizes the geographic distribution of restaurants across India, where each colored dot represents a restaurant and the color corresponds to the respective city. This gives a clear idea of how restaurants are spread across different regions, with noticeable clusters in metropolitan areas like Delhi, Mumbai, Bangalore, Chennai, and Kolkata. The second map provides a density-based view by showing the number of restaurants per city, represented by varying sizes and colors of circles. Larger and brighter circles \(towards yellow\) indicate cities with a higher concentration of restaurants, such as Chennai, Bangalore, and New Delhi, while smaller dark circles show cities with fewer restaurants. Together, these maps highlight both the widespread presence of Zomato-listed restaurants across India and the dominance of certain urban centers as major hubs for food services.)
/E (The first map visualizes the geographic distribution of restaurants across India, where each colored dot represents a restaurant and the color corresponds to the respective city. This gives a clear idea of how restaurants are spread across different regions, with noticeable clusters in metropolitan areas like Delhi, Mumbai, Bangalore, Chennai, and Kolkata. The second map provides a density-based view by showing the number of restaurants per city, represented by varying sizes and colors of circles. Larger and brighter circles \(towards yellow\) indicate cities with a higher concentration of restaurants, such as Chennai, Bangalore, and New Delhi, while smaller dark circles show cities with fewer restaurants. Together, these maps highlight both the widespread presence of Zomato-listed restaurants across India and the dominance of certain urban centers as major hubs for food services.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
